{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_phase2_reconciliation", "label": "Chromatic Intent \u00d7 Design Principles \u2014 Phase 2 Reconciliation (July 2026)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The adjudication record reconciling the live token system against the law layer: every accepted change in a change table, every rejected principle with its reason. Notable rejections: 800-weight hero triad (display voice is deliberately light), strict 1.5\u20131.6 body leading (airy premium voice kept), warm-tinted greyscale (engineered 0%-S neutrality is the identity)."}, {"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_dark_chroma_cap", "label": "Dark-Mode Chroma Cap (C8 Adapted)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Instead of C8's full \u221220\u201330% chroma cut, dark accents are capped at the light variant's OKLCH chroma \u2014 preserving audited dark vibrancy while killing amplification (the principle's actual mechanism). Orange trimmed from C 0.168\u21920.134, green from 0.146\u21920.100; contrast re-verified \u22656.6:1 on #121212."}, {"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_pointer_coarse_targets", "label": "Pointer-Coarse 44px Targets (CI1 Adapted)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "44px enforced where tap errors happen (coarse pointers, via pointer-coarse: variants); compact fine-pointer sizes kept \u2014 mouse precision doesn't need 44px and the compact sizes are part of the visual language."}, {"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_oklch_working_space", "label": "OKLCH as Canonical Color-Reasoning Space", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every new/changed color token is decided and verified in OKLCH (perceptual chroma/lightness + measured WCAG contrast), then authored in HSL. Authored-format migration deferred \u2014 rewriting 100+ working tokens is churn with zero visual delta. Gives C2's law a named working space."}, {"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_gradient_tiering", "label": "Gradient Key Tiering (Core / Reserve / Editorial)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No key deleted: core keys (iris/ember/forest/mint) are the only ones sections may use; reserve keys need a world match; editorial keys fenced to MDX <Mark> + the playground. neon/candy flagged for retirement if still unused at next audit."}, {"id": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_trend_verification", "label": "Phase 3 \u2014 2026 Trend Verification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filter: relevant to Altruvex \u2192 passes through the existing language \u2192 strengthens 'precision engineering'; all three or it's out. Adopted OKLCH reasoning + DTCG tokens as export path; rejected dopamine palettes, neo-brutalism, neumorphism, kinetic type, experimental nav, 3D/WebGL (spectacle spends the sub-1s performance budget on decoration)."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_phase2_reconciliation", "target": "design_design_system_reference", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "header", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_phase2_reconciliation", "target": "docs_design_principles_law_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "header (rule IDs refer to design-principles.md)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_dark_chroma_cap", "target": "docs_design_principles_c8_dark_chroma", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 change table (C8 adapted)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_dark_chroma_cap", "target": "design_color_worlds", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 modifies .dark .accent-world-orange / -green tokens", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_pointer_coarse_targets", "target": "docs_design_principles_ci1_target_size", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 change table (CI1 adapted)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_oklch_working_space", "target": "docs_design_principles_c2_hsl_not_luminance", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design-reconciliation-2026-07.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 (C2's law now has a named working space)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_oklch_working_space", "target": "docs_design_reconciliation_2026_07_dark_chroma_cap", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/de